# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — venue-tree layout (2026-07-28 restructure)
#
# LEGACY-FIRST, and that is deliberate: the restructure moved tracked CODE and
# left the ~20 GB gitignored research substrate physically where it already was
# (`backtest/data`, `backtest/cache`, `backtest/optimize_runs`,
# `backtest/features/nx_v1`). Both path families are therefore ignored here —
# the LEGACY block keeps every existing checkout clean, the NEW block keeps a
# fresh clone clean once writers start landing bytes at the new paths. Deleting
# the legacy block would expose 290k+ untracked files in any current checkout;
# deleting the new block would let a fresh clone commit multi-GB parquets.
# The resolution order itself lives in polymarket/backtest/__init__.py.
#
# Rules are directory-level wherever the whole directory is regenerable.
# =============================================================================

# -- Local dev / runtime state ------------------------------------------------
results/
# local dev DBs + models (config.DATA_ROOT default) — no inline comments here:
# git treats "#" as a comment only at line start, so trailing text breaks the rule
/data/
/logs/
*.log
polymarket/dashboard/snapshot.json
polymarket/dashboard/live-fixture.json

# -- Research substrate: LEGACY paths (physically real in every checkout today)
backtest/data/
backtest/cache/
backtest/features/nx_v1/
backtest/optimize_runs/

# -- Research substrate: NEW paths (what a fresh clone will write) ------------
polymarket/backtest/data/
polymarket/backtest/cache/
polymarket/backtest/features/nx_v1/
polymarket/backtest/optimize_runs/
predictfun/backtest/data/
kalshi/backtest/data/

# The ship-to-live artifact boundary. The heavy binaries are build outputs of
# polymarket/backtest/{build,training}; the small *_manifest.json / provenance
# files beside them stay TRACKED so a checkout records what shipped.
polymarket/backtest/artifacts/*.parquet
polymarket/backtest/artifacts/*.joblib
# The retired LUT's sidecar is a SIBLING FILE, not a directory:
# `<parquet-name>.lutcache.pkl`, so it does not end in .parquet and a
# `lutcache/` dir rule never matched anything. Kept ignored so a stale sidecar
# left over from before the 2026-07-31 retirement still can't be committed.
polymarket/backtest/artifacts/*.lutcache.pkl

# -- Platform console (local mission control) ---------------------------------
# The run archive: history.db (every button-run, the drift graphs' substrate)
# plus history/runs/<run_id>/{log.txt,report.*}. Local operator state, never
# shipped and never committed. config/local.json IS tracked — it is the
# machine map, and it holds no secrets by contract.
platform/history.db
platform/history/

# -- Deploy tarballs (staged bundles; legacy + new infra home) ----------------
deploy/*.tar.gz
polymarket/infra/*.tar.gz
predictfun/infra/*.tar.gz
kalshi/infra/*.tar.gz

# -- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.pytest-gate-tmp/

# -- Env / IDE ----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
.env
.vscode/
.idea/

# -- Local agent workspaces and generated optimization transcripts ------------
.claude/
.context/

# -- Secrets: SSH / TLS keys, AWS deploy key — never commit -------------------
*.pem
*.pem.pub
*.key

# -- Retired-venue DB archives pulled from boxes (large binaries, never commit)
predictfun/archive/

# -- Playwright MCP screenshots + traces (local dev artifacts) ----------------
.playwright-mcp/
dashboard-*.png
tab-*.png

# -- pytest basetemp (see pyproject addopts; default temp root is ACL-locked)
.pytest_tmp/
